stateDiagram-v2
    [*] --> Unauthenticated

    Unauthenticated --> SigningIn: login(actorId)
    SigningIn --> Authenticated: login valid / persist session
    SigningIn --> Unauthenticated: invalid response or request/storage failure

    Unauthenticated --> Authenticated: restore valid persisted session
    Unauthenticated --> Expired: restore expired persisted session
    Expired --> Refreshing: refresh token available
    Expired --> Unauthenticated: no refresh token / clear persisted session

    Authenticated --> Expired: expiresAt reached
    Authenticated --> Refreshing: protected request returns 401
    Expired --> Refreshing: obtain valid session
    Refreshing --> Authenticated: refresh succeeds / persist rotated tokens
    Refreshing --> Unauthenticated: refresh fails / clear memory and storage

    Authenticated --> LoggingOut: logout
    SigningIn --> LoggingOut: logout
    Expired --> LoggingOut: logout
    Refreshing --> LoggingOut: logout / invalidate in-flight refresh
    Unauthenticated --> LoggingOut: logout
    LoggingOut --> Unauthenticated: persisted credentials deleted
    LoggingOut --> LoggingOut: storage deletion fails / report error

    note right of LoggingOut
        Credentials are removed from memory before storage deletion.
        A late login or refresh response cannot restore the session.
        Do not report logout success until storage deletion completes.
    end note

    note right of Authenticated
        The access and refresh tokens are stored with Expo SecureStore.
        Tokens are never written to logs.
    end note
